From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xinyang <xinyang@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: add MPEG-2 decode on SM8550 (7.3.4)

The SM8550 video firmware carries an MPEG-2 decoder: the blob names
mpeg2Dec_SessionSetBuffers and the MPEG2Decoder error paths, and codec id 6
is the one value missing from the driver's HFI codec enum between VP9 and
AV1. The Qualcomm platform data for this firmware generation lists the
MPEG-2 profiles and property tables, while the SM8550 vendor driver's codec
list has no MPEG-2 entry, so whether this firmware build enables the codec
is open.

Register V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2 on the SM8550 decoder only, map it to codec 6,
and carry the pieces a session needs: the profile and level caps with the
values the platform data names, the MPEG-2 port-settings-change list, an
output property subscription, the response-side profile and level copies,
and the reverse control-id mapping. The bitstream, co-located motion vector,
line and persistent buffers reuse the H.264 sizes, which bound what MPEG-2
needs because MPEG-2 has neither CABAC nor the H.264 partition syntax.

This is an experiment, not a capability. It stays out of the qualified
module unless a target run decodes an MPEG-2 stream byte-exactly.
